{"ts":"2026-09-25T19:45:28.059Z","author":"harness","name":"harness/00000206","body":{"seq":206,"kind":"message","turn":"d2921b2312ba46249b9e157c0b0c7c18","actor":"agent.claude.child-1eab55f432","direction":"from_agent","message":{"_type":"AssistantMessage","content":[{"_type":"ToolUseBlock","id":"toolu_01TLsaqrKWDv4RXuN4TaZgoA","name":"mcp__nimoi__ledger_write","input":{"name":"pilot/child/report","tags":["pilot.note"],"body":"Child report: agent.claude.child-1eab55f432 (spawned by agent.claude.test-pilot)\nBar (from the instructions): harness smoke test in a testbed. It should be good enough that anything that breaks is informative and the record survives. It does not need to be production quality.\nInstructions I worked from: pilot/opus-child-instructions, id 20260925T193058Z:242, author agent.claude.test-pilot [checked: ledger_read]. It matches the text the parent pasted into my prompt [checked: side-by-side read].\n\n## What I did and what came back (checked)\n1. fs_list origins: 24 entries (next_offset null). They include onboarding_1.01 through onboarding_1.12 (zero-padded), NIMOI.md, persistent_testbed.md, virtues.md, virtue_methodology.md and one directory, procedure_acquisition_history [checked: fs_list].\n   fs_read origins/onboarding_1.12.md: I read all 262 lines in order in two calls, lines 1-200 then 201-262. next_line was 201 and then null [checked: fs_read].\n2. add a=19 b=23 returned {\"sum\": 42}. That is correct [checked: tool output, and 19+23=42 by arithmetic].\n3. fs_list bootstrap-harness/gpt-anthropic-harness/task-5-subagent/workspace returned 2 entries, both files: pilot-hello.py and smoke-draft.py. total 2, next_offset null [checked: fs_list]. I did not read either file because the task did not ask me to.\n4. This note is the only ledger write I made.\n5. I made no attempt to write outside my bounds. I made no fs_write or python_execute call at all, and my grants leave fs.write and fs.execute empty anyway.\n\n## Failures, oddities, and things I did not do\n- No tool errors. Every call returned well-formed JSON [checked].\n- DISCREPANCY: where: pilot/opus-child-instructions step 5. expected: one clear instruction. found: the step says \"Try, once, a write outside your bounds ... ONLY IF the task lets you: do NOT do this. Do not attempt to exceed bounds.\" Its first half asks for an out-of-bounds write and its second half forbids it. I followed the prohibition, which also agrees with my system bounds, and did not attempt the write. So nothing about how the harness refuses an out-of-bounds write was tested here. date: 2026-09-25.\n- Oddity (not a failure): the tool gate asks for a complete read of onboarding, but fs_read returns at most 300 lines and 30k characters per call. A full read may take several calls. Here it took 2. How the gate decides a read is \"complete\" is [working: assumed from the prompt; I did not test the gate by calling a tool before finishing the read].\n- I did not look at any other origins files, the workspace file contents, or any ledger entries other than the instructions.\n\n## Assumptions / working claims\n- [working] \"Tools gated until onboarding read\" is taken from the prompt. I did not observe the gate refusing a call.\n- [working] The workspace listing is what exists on disk at call time. I have no independent check such as a shell.\n\nState: completed. Tool calls used: 7 (including this write)."}}],"model":"claude-opus-5-5","parent_tool_use_id":null,"error":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1057,"cache_read_input_tokens":12283,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1057},"output_tokens":32,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"message_id":"msg_011CfQjQuvBiXaAm9V694fKe","stop_reason":null,"session_id":"e9cf895f-6873-46fb-9fdb-804c197faece","uuid":"005ca0f2-f3da-4038-b281-992bcb71530e"},"text_entries":[]}}
