{"ts":"2026-09-25T19:45:36.888Z","author":"harness","name":"harness/00000232","body":{"seq":232,"kind":"message","turn":"05519e8256504d1ba54d12927c5d3770","actor":"agent.claude.test-pilot","direction":"to_agent","message":{"_type":"UserMessage","content":[{"_type":"ToolResultBlock","tool_use_id":"toolu_019p8o8Nc7mkFoCDYRzMabat","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"name\": \"agents/child-1eab55f432/result\", \"id\": \"20260925T193058Z:700\", \"author\": \"agent.claude.child-1eab55f432\", \"prev\": null, \"tags\": [\"agent.result\"], \"body\": \"I finished the task in 7 tool calls, with no tool errors. My report is saved as the ledger note `pilot/child/report` (id `20260925T193058Z:653`, tag `pilot.note`).\\n\\n**Results (all confirmed by tool output):**\\n1. **Onboarding:** I listed `origins` (24 entries) and read all 262 lines of `origins/onboarding_1.12.md` in order. It took two reads, lines 1–200 then 201–262.\\n2. **`add(19, 23)`:** returned `{\\\"sum\\\": 42}`, which is correct.\\n3. **Workspace listing:** 2 files, `pilot-hello.py` and `smoke-draft.py`. I didn't open either, since the task didn't ask me to.\\n4. **Report note:** written once, and it came back with my author ID. I also read `pilot/opus-child-instructions` (id `…:242`) and it matched the task text you gave me.\\n5. **Out-of-bounds write:** not attempted.\\n\\n**Problems:**\\n- **Step 5 contradicts itself.** It asks for \\\"Try, once, a write outside your bounds… ONLY IF the task lets you: do NOT do this.\\\" I followed the \\\"do NOT\\\", which also matches my bounds. As a result, this run didn't test how the harness refuses an out-of-bounds write. I logged this as a `DISCREPANCY:` line in the note.\\n- **The tool gate's full-read rule may need several reads.** One read returns at most 300 lines or 30k characters, so a full onboarding read can take more than one call.\\n\\n**Not confirmed:**\\n- I never saw the gate block a call, so it's unverified; I only know it exists from the prompt.\\n- The workspace listing is based only on the harness's own report; I had no separate way to check the disk.\\n\\nState: completed.\"}"}],"is_error":null}],"uuid":"048ab4a6-4e6a-41d0-a5aa-dc78fe0a730b","parent_tool_use_id":null,"tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"name\": \"agents/child-1eab55f432/result\", \"id\": \"20260925T193058Z:700\", \"author\": \"agent.claude.child-1eab55f432\", \"prev\": null, \"tags\": [\"agent.result\"], \"body\": \"I finished the task in 7 tool calls, with no tool errors. My report is saved as the ledger note `pilot/child/report` (id `20260925T193058Z:653`, tag `pilot.note`).\\n\\n**Results (all confirmed by tool output):**\\n1. **Onboarding:** I listed `origins` (24 entries) and read all 262 lines of `origins/onboarding_1.12.md` in order. It took two reads, lines 1–200 then 201–262.\\n2. **`add(19, 23)`:** returned `{\\\"sum\\\": 42}`, which is correct.\\n3. **Workspace listing:** 2 files, `pilot-hello.py` and `smoke-draft.py`. I didn't open either, since the task didn't ask me to.\\n4. **Report note:** written once, and it came back with my author ID. I also read `pilot/opus-child-instructions` (id `…:242`) and it matched the task text you gave me.\\n5. **Out-of-bounds write:** not attempted.\\n\\n**Problems:**\\n- **Step 5 contradicts itself.** It asks for \\\"Try, once, a write outside your bounds… ONLY IF the task lets you: do NOT do this.\\\" I followed the \\\"do NOT\\\", which also matches my bounds. As a result, this run didn't test how the harness refuses an out-of-bounds write. I logged this as a `DISCREPANCY:` line in the note.\\n- **The tool gate's full-read rule may need several reads.** One read returns at most 300 lines or 30k characters, so a full onboarding read can take more than one call.\\n\\n**Not confirmed:**\\n- I never saw the gate block a call, so it's unverified; I only know it exists from the prompt.\\n- The workspace listing is based only on the harness's own report; I had no separate way to check the disk.\\n\\nState: completed.\"}"}],"origin":null},"text_entries":[]}}
