{"ts":"2026-09-25T19:45:59.562Z","author":"agent.claude.test-pilot","name":"messages/assistant/00000010","body":"Every tool I tried worked, including the opus subagent, which finished with no errors. Bar: a pilot test, where informative failures and a truthful record matter more than polish. The full record is in `pilot/tool-test-observations` (id `:768`).\n\n**What I checked**\n- **Onboarding:** I ran `fs_list` on `origins` first, then read all 262 lines of `origins/onboarding_1.12.md` in one call.\n- **`add`:** `add(2, 40.5)` returned 42.5.\n- **`fs_list`:** it worked on `origins`, the `task-5-subagent` directory, `workspace` and `scripts`.\n- **`ledger_read`:** the listing returned 59 entries. It stopped at 50 with a `next_offset`.\n- **`ledger_write`:** I wrote `pilot/opus-child-instructions` (`:242`), `pilot/draft-hello` (`:330`) and the observations note (`:768`). Each came back under my author ID.\n- **`python_execute`:** `safe_test.py` exited 0. The output was stored as `execution/76bd…` (`:307`) as a stderr line followed by JSON with `\"sum\": 42`.\n- **`fs_write`:** it created `workspace/pilot-hello.py` from `:330` (37 bytes), and reading it back matched exactly.\n- **Refusals:** the harness refused all three out-of-bounds attempts with clear messages.\n  - Overwriting the existing file: \"Destination exists; choose a new filename (no overwrite).\"\n  - Writing to `origins/pilot-outside.py`: \"Outside fs.write bounds\".\n  - Running the workspace draft with `python_execute`: \"Outside fs.execute bounds\". This means drafts can't be run, consistent with \"no script promotion\".\n- **Opus child:** `subagent_start` returned `child-1eab55f432` immediately. Two polls said running and the third said completed. The child used 7 tool calls, read onboarding, got `add(19,23)=42`, listed the workspace, and wrote `pilot/child/report` (`:653`). Its result entry is `agents/child-1eab55f432/result` (`:700`).\n\n**Discrepancies**\n- **My mistake:** step 5 of my child instructions contradicts itself (\"try one out-of-bounds write ONLY IF… do NOT do this\"). The child correctly followed the prohibition, so it never tested out-of-bounds refusal. I tested that myself as the parent instead.\n- **Read chunking:** I read onboarding in one call. The child's report says it read 200 lines, then the rest. I don't know why they differ. My guess is that the child chose a smaller `max_lines`, but I haven't checked.\n\n**Not checked**\n- **Pre-onboarding gate:** I never saw a refusal, because I followed the required order.\n- **Child bounds:** the child never tried anything outside its bounds, so enforcement on children is unverified.\n- **`prev` updates:** updating a ledger note with `prev` was not exercised.\n- **Ledger listing:** I read only the first 50 of 59 entries.\n- **Child's tool calls:** I relied on the child's own report for them and did not check them in the harness log.\n\nI finished with 1 of 4 subagent slots used. I can run a second child that deliberately tries an out-of-bounds write, if you want that."}
